<title>UK: Iran, UAE, Nigeria say at quota in June - OPECNA.</title>
<headline>Iran, UAE, Nigeria say at quota in June - OPECNA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran told OPEC it produced and supplied 3.591 million barrels per day (bpd) in June, within its OPEC allocation of 3.6 million bpd, the OPEC News Agency (OPECNA) said on Friday.</p>
<p>The United Arab Emirates (UAE) told OPEC headquarters in Vienna it produced 2.218 million bpd last month but supplied only 2.155 million bpd, compared with its quota of 2.161 million.</p>
<p>Nigeria said it produced 1.9 million bpd in June but supplied 1.865 million bpd, exactly in line with its allocation.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for June according to member country submissions to the OPEC Secretariat were as follows (in million bpd):</p>
<p>		 Production	 Supply</p>
<p>Algeria	0.802		0.800</p>
<p>Indonesia    1.329		N/A</p>
<p>Iran	   3.591		3.591</p>
<p>Iraq	   0.700		0.700</p>
<p>Kuwait	 2.006		2.006</p>
<p>Libya	  1.398		1.393</p>
<p>Nigeria	1.900		1.865</p>
<p>Qatar	  0.387		0.379</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia 8.007		8.000</p>
<p>UAE	    2.218		2.155</p>
<p>Venezuela    2.415		2.410</p>
<p>N/A - not available</p>
<p>Supply as defined by OPEC is calculated as domestic consumption plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
